WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.606
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade twelve English.

2
00:00:05.906 --> 00:00:09.396
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.696 --> 00:00:15.960
Unit eleven: Linking Words and Connectors. Today you will join ideas with contrast, reason and result.

4
00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.005
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:23.025
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.883 --> 00:00:24.826
However.

7
00:00:25.817 --> 00:00:28.141
However means used to show contrast.

8
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.274
However, it was late.

9
00:00:30.883 --> 00:00:33.327
Your turn. Say: However.

10
00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:37.098
However.

11
00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:38.781
Therefore.

12
00:00:39.783 --> 00:00:41.667
Therefore means as a result.

13
00:00:42.283 --> 00:00:43.540
Therefore, we left.

14
00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:46.698
Your turn. Say: Therefore.

15
00:00:49.533 --> 00:00:50.592
Therefore.

16
00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:52.305
Moreover.

17
00:00:53.317 --> 00:00:55.049
Moreover means in addition.

18
00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:57.232
Moreover, it is cheap.

19
00:00:57.817 --> 00:01:00.504
Your turn. Say: Moreover.

20
00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:04.461
Moreover.

21
00:01:05.217 --> 00:01:06.125
Despite.

22
00:01:07.117 --> 00:01:09.604
Despite means without being affected by.

23
00:01:10.217 --> 00:01:11.961
Despite the rain, we played.

24
00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:15.051
Your turn. Say: Despite.

25
00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:18.924
Despite.

26
00:01:19.683 --> 00:01:20.835
In spite of.

27
00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:23.687
In spite of means even though.

28
00:01:24.283 --> 00:01:26.155
In spite of his age, he ran.

29
00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:29.855
Your turn. Say: In spite of.

30
00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.038
In spite of.

31
00:01:34.783 --> 00:01:35.796
Because of.

32
00:01:36.783 --> 00:01:38.655
Because of means for the reason of.

33
00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:41.342
Because of the storm, we stayed.

34
00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:44.498
Your turn. Say: Because of.

35
00:01:47.333 --> 00:01:48.462
Because of.

36
00:01:49.217 --> 00:01:50.380
As a result.

37
00:01:51.383 --> 00:01:53.162
As a result means therefore.

38
00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:55.529
As a result, he passed.

39
00:01:56.117 --> 00:01:58.467
Your turn. Say: As a result.

40
00:02:01.333 --> 00:02:02.555
As a result.

41
00:02:03.317 --> 00:02:04.178
Whereas.

42
00:02:05.183 --> 00:02:07.322
Whereas means but in contrast.

43
00:02:07.917 --> 00:02:09.719
He is tall whereas she is short.

44
00:02:10.317 --> 00:02:12.656
Your turn. Say: Whereas.

45
00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:16.594
Whereas.

46
00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.784
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:23.812
Visal, how do I show contrast?

48
00:02:24.917 --> 00:02:35.411
Use but, although, however and whereas. Although it was cold, we swam. It was cold; however, we swam. Despite and in spite of are followed by a noun or -ing.

49
00:02:36.517 --> 00:02:38.354
How about reason and result?

50
00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:50.589
Use because and since before a clause, and because of before a noun. For result use so, therefore and as a result: It rained, so we stayed home.

51
00:02:51.683 --> 00:02:53.358
How do I punctuate however?

52
00:02:54.450 --> 00:03:04.721
Put a full stop or semicolon before however and a comma after it: It was late. However, we continued. Do not join two sentences with only a comma.

53
00:03:05.867 --> 00:03:07.437
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:08.283 --> 00:03:11.188
Grammar focus: Connectors by function.

55
00:03:11.488 --> 00:03:12.675
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:13.383 --> 00:03:15.290
Although it was cold, we swam.

57
00:03:16.183 --> 00:03:18.264
Despite the rain, we played football.

58
00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:25.370
Use although with a clause and despite with a noun or -ing. Use therefore and as a result to show a result.

59
00:03:26.117 --> 00:03:30.069
Be careful! Don't say: Despite it rained, we played.

60
00:03:32.033 --> 00:03:34.428
Say: Despite the rain, we played.

61
00:03:34.728 --> 00:03:36.216
Despite + noun.

62
00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.699
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:41.815
A Rainy Match.

64
00:03:42.115 --> 00:03:44.010
It rained heavily on Saturday.

65
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.464
Despite the rain, the team played football.

66
00:03:48.467 --> 00:03:51.256
Although the field was wet, nobody gave up.

67
00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:55.032
They won the match; therefore, they reached the final.

68
00:03:56.033 --> 00:03:58.451
Moreover, the crowd was very happy.

69
00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:03.603
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:06.345
Despite is followed by a blank.

71
00:04:06.645 --> 00:04:10.716
A, full clause. B, verb only. C, noun.

72
00:04:14.267 --> 00:04:16.069
The answer is C: noun.

73
00:04:17.217 --> 00:04:18.903
Although it was cold, we blank.

74
00:04:19.203 --> 00:04:23.390
A, swam. B, but swam. C, so swam.

75
00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:28.619
The answer is A: swam.

76
00:04:29.783 --> 00:04:31.330
Therefore shows a blank.

77
00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:35.574
A, time. B, result. C, contrast.

78
00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:41.226
The answer is B: result.

79
00:04:42.383 --> 00:04:43.907
Whereas shows blank.

80
00:04:44.207 --> 00:04:47.976
A, reason. B, result. C, contrast.

81
00:04:51.533 --> 00:04:53.614
The answer is C: contrast.

82
00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:56.831
Because of is followed by a blank.

83
00:04:57.131 --> 00:05:00.320
A, noun. B, clause. C, verb.

84
00:05:03.867 --> 00:05:05.471
The answer is A: noun.

85
00:05:06.667 --> 00:05:10.016
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:13.305
Join: It was late. We continued.

87
00:05:22.117 --> 00:05:23.640
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:33.015
Although it was late, we continued. I could also write It was late; however, we continued. Both sentences show contrast.

89
00:05:33.315 --> 00:05:35.129
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:36.017 --> 00:05:40.248
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and connectors by function.

91
00:05:40.548 --> 00:05:45.418
Today's value is logical rigor. Follow your reasoning wherever it honestly leads.

92
00:05:45.718 --> 00:05:48.057
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

93
00:05:48.357 --> 00:05:51.346
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

